"Necro" <necro19@wp.pl> writes:

> I got a problem with Linux Version.
> I heard that you can edit one file so you don't have to change controls for
> Numpad every time you start playing. How to do that, what files to edit, and
> how do to this so I won't mess up Nethack?

Use your favorite text editor. The file is called .nethackrc and located
in your home directory. 
If it doesn't exist, you can create one from scratch or copy one from
somewhere. You can start with

OPTIONS=!number_pad,lit_corridor,!rest_on_space

to turn number_pad and rest_on_space off and lit_corridor on.
You should give the world read permissions to the file and execute
permissions to your home directory for the game to be able to read the
file:
chmod a+r ~/.nethackrc
chmod a+x ~

